function privacy(){return simple('Privacy','Your information.<br><em>In your hands.</em>','How this standalone frontend handles your interactions.')+section(`<div class="intro-copy">${featureRows([['Forms stay on this page','Form fields are processed locally in your browser to prepare a downloadable brief. They are not transmitted to FORKLS or any other server. They are cleared when the page is closed or reloaded.'],['Finn is a local guide','Finn answers from a small set of website topics and navigation links. This is not a connected AI service. Messages remain in page memory only.'],['No tracking is included','This file contains its own images, fonts, styles and animation library. It does not include analytics, advertising pixels, cookies or external runtime asset requests.'],['External links have their own policies','Opening the official FORKLS website leaves this frontend. That site handles any information you choose to submit there under its own policies.']])}</div>`);}
function credits(){return simple('Illustration & source notes','A story in ink.<br><em>Grounded in engineering.</em>','Original artwork and source material used in this FORKLS frontend concept.')+section(`<div class="intro-copy"><h3>Company material</h3><p>The two distinct FORKLS logos, engineering blueprint and company-event photography originate from <a class="textlink" href="https://forkls.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">forkls.com</a>. Company and product descriptions are adapted from its public pages. The motor and drone portal structure follows the supplied content plans.</p><h3>Visual direction</h3><p>The cream palette, editorial type, ink illustrations, guide interaction and scroll-led storytelling are inspired by the supplied Five Pathways reference and video. Artwork and the Finn character were generated specifically for this FORKLS concept.</p><h3>Illustrations and technical scope</h3><p>Original generated artwork depicts Canadian ink landscapes, Finn, a motor cutaway, agricultural and mapping missions, and six drone component groups. Frame-by-frame sprite artwork animates a balloon, maple leaves, a compass and a question jar. People photography comes from the original FORKLS website. They are illustrative; they do not establish production specifications, exact assemblies or performance.</p><h3>Libraries and fonts</h3><p>Animation uses embedded anime.js 3.2.2 (MIT). Typography uses Instrument Serif and DM Sans (SIL Open Font License). All required assets are embedded in this HTML.</p></div>`);}
